# Simfree meeting architecture (Cursor context)

## Scale target

- Group meetings (SFU) are built for **at least 10 participants** today.
- We will **gradually increase** capacity (config, mediasoup/VPS tuning, load tests) — do not hard-code “6 users” in new code or docs unless quoting legacy text.
- Current default: `SFU_MAX_PEERS=10` in `src/config/env.ts`, `.env.example`, and `deploy/setup-server.sh`.
- When changing limits, update **backend config**, **API responses** (`maxParticipants`), **docs**, and any admin copy that mentions participant caps.

## Two repos — one product

| Layer | Repo / path | Role |
|-------|-------------|------|
| **Backend** | `D:\videocalling` (this repo) | Fastify API, rooms, signaling WS, mediasoup SFU |
| **Browser SDK (source of truth)** | `D:\videocalling\packages\client-sdk\src\` | `MeetingClient`, types, staff call client |
| **SDK copy (consumer)** | `D:\simfree-monorepo\packages\video-client\src\` | Published in monorepo as `@simfree/video-client` |
| **Admin UI** | `D:\simfree-monorepo\apps\admin\` | Meetings page, `/meet/[code]`, `MeetingRoom.tsx` |

The admin app **does not** embed videocalling server code. It calls the video API over HTTP/WebSocket and imports **`@simfree/video-client`**.

## SDK workflow (required)

1. Implement or fix meeting behavior in **`packages/client-sdk/`** (this repo).
2. Sync to Simfree:
   ```bash
   npm run sync:simfree
   # or: SIMFREE_ROOT=D:/simfree-monorepo bash scripts/sync-sdk-to-simfree.sh
   ```
3. Rebuild consumer package and admin:
   ```bash
   cd D:/simfree-monorepo
   pnpm --filter @simfree/video-client build
   pnpm --filter admin build
   ```
4. Do **not** edit `simfree-monorepo/packages/video-client/src/` as the primary copy — changes will be overwritten on the next sync.

Admin-only UI (layouts, toasts, sounds, forms) lives under `apps/admin/` and does not need to live in the SDK unless it is reusable client logic.

## Backend touchpoints for meetings

- HTTP: `src/routes/meetings.ts` → `src/rooms/room-service.ts`
- Signaling: `src/signaling/` (join, lobby, SFU handlers)
- SFU: `src/sfu/` (mediasoup; one upstream per peer, N downstream)
- Expiry / limits: `src/rooms/meeting-expiry.ts`, `expiresAt`, `durationMinutes`

